Hmm, so predicates, even without zi'o, are not inextricable from their
places. That's interesting, although it stabs the "lojban has a pure logical
core" thing a bit more than it was already stabbed, since predicates are
functions from n-tuples to truth values in formal logic, and having no x4
for klama means you have no 5-tuple that is related by klama.

mu'o mi'e .latros.

